From: Jesse Casco <jesse.casco@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:45:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] LOCAL: arm64: dts: qcom: glymur-asus-zenbook-a16: give the
 HDMI HPD pin to mdss_dp2

The HPD pin (gpio126, usb2_dp) is claimed by the PS185 bridge node. Give it
to the DP controller, as the Glymur CRD does on the same path in
https://github.com/qualcomm-linux/kernel/pull/1493 (open).

Package revision 8 detects an HDMI plug without this change, so it is for
consistency with the CRD. Tested together with the DP PHY series only.

Signed-off-by: Jesse Casco <jesse.casco@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-asus-zenbook-a16-ux3607oa.dts | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-asus-zenbook-a16-ux3607oa.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-asus-zenbook-a16-ux3607oa.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-asus-zenbook-a16-ux3607oa.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-asus-zenbook-a16-ux3607oa.dts
@@ -77,9 +77,6 @@
 	hdmi-bridge {
 		compatible = "parade,ps185hdm";
 
-		pinctrl-0 = <&usb2_dp_hot_plug_detect>;
-		pinctrl-names = "default";
-
 		ports {
 			#address-cells = <1>;
 			#size-cells = <0>;
@@ -984,6 +981,9 @@
 };
 
 &mdss_dp2 {
+	pinctrl-0 = <&usb2_dp_hot_plug_detect>;
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
